      "title": "I can't stop thinking about Papua New Guinea",
      "type": "story",
      "url": "https://notnottalmud.substack.com/p/why-i-cant-stop-thinking-about-papua",
      "og_image": "https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!o2BG!,w_1200,h_675,c_fill,f_jpg,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep,g_auto/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F1cf2320c-0d17-4c36-bf55-4372c97e32e4_3099x3069.jpeg",
      "groq_label": "Papua New Guinea presents extreme physical and technological isolation, where Mount Hagen hosts the world's highest-latency internet servers and urban violence includes arrow attacks.",
      "groq_discussion": "Discussion type: – Short:\n\nThis blog post addresses the unique cultural, historical, and living conditions of Papua New Guinea. Hacker News commenters generally appreciated the shared personal anecdotes and documentary recommendations and believed the project could provide valuable perspective on extreme global differences in standards of living. However, they also expressed concerns about safety risks and harsh living conditions and questioned the travel logistics and safety of visiting the region. Overall, the discussion was mixed, with commenters recognizing both the project's potential and its limitations.",
      "groq_explain": null
    },
